<h2>Which vision test should you take?</h2>
<p>To check how sharp your eyesight is, use the <a href="/eye-test/">eye test</a>. It draws a tumbling E chart at the right size for your distance, after a one-minute calibration with a bank card, and gives your score per eye in the familiar 20/20 or 6/6 form. The <a href="/astigmatism-test/">astigmatism test</a> is a clock dial: if the lines in one direction look darker with one eye, that points to astigmatism, a very common reason for blurred or doubled letters.</p>
<p>For color, start with the <a href="/red-green-color-blind-test/">red-green color blind test</a>: twelve dot plates in the style of the Ishihara test, with two plates that separate the protan (red) and deutan (green) types. The <a href="/color-vision-test/">color vision test</a> works like the Farnsworth D-15: you put colored caps in order around the color circle, which also shows blue-yellow (tritan) problems and how strong a deficiency is. The <a href="/blind-spot-test/">blind spot test</a> shows the natural blind spot every eye has, and measures where it sits.</p>

<h2>How to get a fair result at home</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Calibrate</strong> the screen where a test asks you to. A browser does not know the size of your screen, and letter sizes and angles depend on it.</li>
<li><strong>Turn off color filters:</strong> Night Light, Night Shift, True Tone, Eye Comfort, blue light glasses and dark-mode tints all change colors.</li>
<li><strong>Measure the distance</strong> with a tape and keep browser zoom at 100%.</li>
<li><strong>Test one eye at a time</strong>, covering the other with your palm without pressing. The better eye hides a weaker one when both are open.</li>
<li><strong>Use good light</strong> and full screen brightness, and take the test when your eyes are not tired.</li>
</ul>

<h2>When to see an eye doctor</h2>
<p>Book a full eye examination every two years, or every year for children, people over 60 and people with diabetes, even if online tests look fine: many eye diseases cause no symptoms until late. Book sooner if a test here shows a result worse than 20/40 in either eye, a clear difference between the eyes, signs of astigmatism or color blindness you did not know about, or if your vision has changed. Seek urgent care the same day for sudden vision loss, a curtain or shadow over part of your sight, new floaters with flashes, double vision or a painful red eye.</p>

